KAN-100 — How to Use the Speed/Cost Weight Parameter

The parameter speed_weight controls the solver objective:
  0.0 = minimize cost only (default)
  1.0 = minimize duration only
  0.5 = equal blend of cost and duration

--- Quick test (hardcode) ---

1. Open core/solver_service.h
2. Change the default value on this line:
     double speedWeight = 0.0;  // set to 0.0–1.0
3. Rebuild and run:
     cd core/build
     make -j$(nproc)
     ./solver_regression_test

--- Run server with env var ---

  SPEED_WEIGHT=0.7 ./solver

This sets speedWeight via environment variable at startup.
The env var only applies when the caller does not set speed_weight in the proto request.

--- Set per-request in C++ tests ---

  solver::SolveRequest req;
  req.set_speed_weight(0.7);
  SolverV2 solver;
  auto resp = solver.Solve(req);

--- What to observe ---

Run with speedWeight=0.0 and speedWeight=1.0 and compare:
  - objective= in [Solve] log line  →  changes scale (THB vs minutes)
  - total_duration on routes        →  lower when weight=1.0
  - total_cost on routes            →  lower when weight=0.0

--- Wire Go→C++ transport (requires internet) ---

  go generate ./solver/proto/
  # then in solver/grpc/convert.go, inside problemToProto():
  req.SpeedWeight = p.SpeedWeight
